! ja_ax1a "IBOX-1", routines IBIN35-IBIN55, pp.25-26 (octal 004062.00-
! 004107.40): the three "RESTART OF ROUTINE" sections that test BRANCH
! ON XL, XE and XH -- the whole tail of "BRANCH ON I BOX INDICATORS",
! up to where "COMPARE VALUE %KV%" begins.
!
! WHY THIS BLOCK IS DIFFERENT from the five groups in ibox1_bind.strap.
! Those reach their indicators through an index LOAD: XF, XCZ, XVLZ,
! XVZ and XVGZ are all side effects of LX, so the deck sets them by
! choosing a seed word.  XL is not.  It is an index COMPARISON
! indicator, and no index load touches it -- so to test the branch, the
! deck has to put the bit there BY HAND:
!
!   LX, $X1, IBXWZ        set XW to zero
!   LV, $X1, IBXWZ6       load bit 20, %XL IND%
!   SV, $X1, $IND+.32     store in IND reg.
!
! That last line is the point.  $IND is word 11, the INDICATOR
! REGISTER, and SV stores the 24-bit value field at a BIT address, so
! the store covers IBM bits 32-55 of word 11.  IBXWZ6's value has bit
! 20 set, and 32 + 20 = 52, which is XL.  The deck is poking an
! indicator through ordinary storage -- the Reference Card's footnote c
! says only indicator bits 0-19 are read-only, and this is what that
! permission is for.
!
! THE SAME SHAPE THREE TIMES, with one constant changing.  IBXWZ6 has
! value bit 20, IBXWZ7 bit 21, IBXWZ8 bit 22, and 32 + 20/21/22 = 52,
! 53, 54 = XL, XE, XH -- three consecutive indicator bits poked through
! three consecutive value bits.  All three reuse IBXWZ, the all-zero
! index word the listing calls "COMMON XW".  That the same store lands
! on three different bits is what makes the group worth transcribing
! whole rather than stopping at XL: a fold that were off by one in the
! bit position would pass none of them, but one that mishandled the
! half-word boundary could pass one and not the others.
!
! So the blocks pin two things nothing else does: the indicator
! register being WRITABLE as ordinary storage above bit 19, and the
! branch-on-indicator machinery over an indicator that no index
! operation sets.  The BZXL/BXL/BZXLZ sequence is the same grammar as
! the five groups -- leading Z branches if the bit is OFF, trailing Z
! turns it off after testing.
!
! The routine ends after IBIN55; the next page begins "COMPARE VALUE
! %KV%", which is a different test.

        SLC, (8)4062.0
IBIN35  LX, $X1, IBXWZ                       ! set XW to zero
        LV, $X1, IBXWZ6                      ! load bit 20, %XL IND%
        SV, $X1, $IND+.32                    ! store in IND reg.
IBIN36  BZXL, $                              ! hang up if bit off
IBIN37  BXL, $+1.0                           ! dont branch if bit off
        BD, $                                ! hang up if no branch
IBIN38  BZXLZ, $                             ! hang up if bit off or turn off
IBIN39  BXL, $                               ! hang up if bit on
IBIN40  BZXL, $+1.0                          ! branch if bit off
        BD, $                                ! hang up if bit on
        B, IBIN41                            ! branch out
IBXWZ6  VF, (8)0.10                          ! equals %XL IND%
IBXWZ   XW, 0, 0, 0, 0                       ! common XW
IBIN41  VF, (8)777777.70                     ! executed as NOP,-.32
        VF, (8)777777.70                     ! executed as NOP,-.32
!
! ---- XE: same poke, value bit 21 -> indicator bit 53 -------------
IBIN42  LX, $X1, IBXWZ                       ! set XW to zero
        LV, $X1, IBXWZ7                      ! load bit 21, %XE IND%
        SV, $X1, $IND+.32                    ! store in IND reg.
IBIN43  BZXE, $                              ! hang up if bit off
IBIN44  BXE, $+1.0                           ! dont branch if bit off
        BD, $                                ! hang up if no branch
IBIN45  BZXEZ, $                             ! hang up if bit off or turn off
IBIN46  BXE, $                               ! hang up if bit on
IBIN47  BZXE, $+1.0                          ! branch if bit off
        BD, $                                ! hang up if bit on
        B, IBIN48                            ! branch out
IBXWZ7  VF, (8)0.04                          ! equals %XE IND%
IBIN48  VF, (8)777777.70                     ! executed as NOP,-.32
        VF, (8)777777.70                     ! executed as NOP,-.32
!
! ---- XH: same poke, value bit 22 -> indicator bit 54 -------------
IBIN49  LX, $X1, IBXWZ                       ! set XW to zero
        LV, $X1, IBXWZ8                      ! load bit 22, %XH IND%
        SV, $X1, $IND+.32                    ! store in IND reg.
IBIN50  BZXH, $                              ! hang up if bit off
IBIN51  BXH, $+1.0                           ! dont branch if bit off
        BD, $                                ! hang up if no branch
IBIN52  BZXHZ, $                             ! hang up if bit off or turn off
IBIN53  BXH, $                               ! hang up if bit on
IBIN54  BZXH, $+1.0                          ! branch if bit off
        BD, $                                ! hang up if bit on
        B, IBIN55                            ! branch out
IBXWZ8  VF, (8)0.02                          ! equals %XH IND%
IBIN55  VF, (8)777777.70                     ! executed as NOP,-.32
        VF, (8)777777.70                     ! executed as NOP,-.32
PASS    BEW, $
        END, IBIN35
